        itemId = 54465,
        name = "Vashj'ir Seahorse",
        mountCategory = "Quest Rewards",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - A short introductory quest chain and a guided riding minigame give a guaranteed reward.\n\n1. Start the original Vashj'ir introduction. Alliance can take Call of Duty from Recruiter Burns at Stormwind Harbor (27.4,24.5). Horde follows Warchief's Command: Vashj'ir! to Commander Thorak at Bladefist Bay (55.8,12.2 in Durotar). Board the quest ship and let the shipwreck sequence finish.\n\n2. Complete Sea Legs with Erunak Stonespeaker, then the opening survival and shelter quests in Kelp'thar Forest. Continue the quests from Erunak and the nearby survivors rather than swimming straight to the mount objective: the later quest giver is phased until this introduction advances.\n\n3. Find Moanah Stormhoof at Shallow's End, around 46.0,46.8. Complete Better Late Than Dead and Sea-Food Chain when offered, then accept The Abyssal Ride. If she has no quests, finish the outstanding opening-hub quests first.\n\n4. Dismiss a summoned companion pet if the lure fails to appear. Click the coil of rope beside Moanah at the edge of the drop, select its lure interaction once, then approach and mount the seahorse that swims to it. Repeatedly clicking the rope can interrupt the setup.\n\n5. During the ride, use the quest's three arrow buttons or their displayed action-bar bindings, normally 1, 2 and 3. Follow each on-screen lean or grip prompt when it appears; ordinary movement keys do not operate those vehicle actions. If thrown off, return and try the rope again.\n\n6. Turn in The Abyssal Ride and learn the seahorse reward if an item is provided. Summon it in Vashj'ir on the character that completed the chain. Other characters must do their own introduction and mount quest.",
