        name = "Fossilized Raptor",
        mountCategory = "Other",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Level Archaeology and repeat random Fossil projects; there is no guaranteed discovery count.\n\n1. Learn Archaeology from Harrison Jones in Stormwind Keep (85.7,25.9) or Belloc Brightblade in Orgrimmar (49.0,70.6). Open the Archaeology window and enable dig sites on the world map.\n\n2. For the direct route, survey Fossil sites in Eastern Kingdoms or Kalimdor. Use Survey inside the marked dig-site boundary, follow its direction indicator, and move shorter distances as it changes from red to yellow to green. Finish other sites when necessary to generate new Fossil sites; the locations rotate.\n\n3. Solve the currently offered Fossil project whenever you have enough fragments. Continue until Fossilized Raptor appears, collect the 100 fragments it requests, solve it and use the completed mount item.\n\n4. To use fragment crates instead of searching for continental Fossil sites, first raise Archaeology to 600. Broken Isles archaeology can provide skill and Restored Artifacts, but its active excavation zone rotates; Azsuna is not permanently available. Pandaria and other expansion solves that can be crated are alternatives.\n\n5. To focus Pandaria sites, reach Exalted with the Lorewalkers and visit Brann Bronzebeard at the Seat of Knowledge above Mogu'shan Palace (83.5,31.0 in the Vale). Buy a Mantid Artifact Hunter's Kit for 2 Restored Artifacts, open it when ready to dig and use its Lorewalker's Map with the Sonic Locator effect active.\n\n6. Survey the resulting Mantid sites in Townlong Steppes and Dread Wastes. Solve common Mantid artifacts and turn the completed objects into Restored Artifacts. Return to Brann and exchange these for Crates of Fossil Archaeology Fragments, not Tol'vir or Troll crates.\n\n7. Open the Fossil crates and keep solving Fossil projects as in step 3. The final project can appear early or after many solves. Neither the Mantid route nor reaching maximum skill guarantees the next project will be the mount.",
