        itemId = 62900,
        name = "Volcanic Stone Drake",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 27,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Several bosses must survive for add mechanics; daily Heroic lockouts and excessive high-level damage can force repeat visits.\n\n1. Set Dungeon Difficulty to Heroic and open Glory of the Cataclysm Hero (4845). Plan to complete every unfinished challenge below, plus Cataclysm Dungeon Hero (4844). Read the relevant setup BEFORE hitting a boss: killing it too early usually means another character or the next daily Heroic reset.\n\n2. BLACKROCK CAVERNS: enter Blackrock Mountain from Burning Steppes or Searing Gorge. On the east side of the inner ring take the Blackrock Spire hallway, then its right-hand branch into Caverns (Burning Steppes map about 27.4,27.9). The route is inside the mountain, not on its outside summit.\n\n3. Rom'ogg - Crushing Bones and Cracking Skulls: keep him alive while Quake produces Angered Earth adds. At high level, remove gear and /sit for Quake to help it actually hit and spawn adds; bring a lower-level helper if the spawns still fail. Keep the adds alive and gather them near him. At his roughly 66% and 33% health transitions, free yourself from Chains of Woe and let The Skullcracker kill the gathered adds. Get ten add deaths credited to HIS attack before finishing him; your AoE kills do not count.\n\n4. For a max-level Rom'ogg attempt, the recent Midnight comment uses Oil of Immolation (8956) with gear removed to cross each health threshold without one-shotting him. Gather at least five adds, separate them from the boss, allow only one oil tick, and immediately cancel the buff. Its exact damage depends on your character: watch his health rather than treating the reported percentage as guaranteed. Let Skullcracker kill that wave, wait out the oil cooldown and repeat for ten total. Do not leave the oil running on the adds.\n\n5. Corla - Arrested Development: let all three kneeling zealots finish evolving into Twilight Drakonids; do not block every beam or kill zealots before evolution. Kill each evolved drakonid, then Corla. Karsh - Too Hot to Handle: move him into the central lava column and wait until his Superheated Quicksilver Armor has at least 15 stacks, then kill him before the stacks expire. Obsidius - Ascendant Descending: kill him promptly before anyone reaches four stacks of Crepuscular Veil; kite his shadow copies if necessary.\n\n6. THE STONECORE: fly to the portal on the Temple of Earth's upper exterior ledge in Deepholm (47.5,52.1). For Rotten to the Core, leave the Devout Followers near High Priestess Azil alive. Body-pull the preceding room and the three packs in front of her, gathering at least 60. Pull Azil with a non-damaging ability, then kill the followers within ten seconds of the pull. Do not kill those packs while walking in and do not kill Azil before triggering their count. Finish the Heroic dungeon.\n\n7. THE VORTEX PINNACLE: fly to the airborne portal in southeast Uldum at 76.8,84.4. You need Extra Credit Bonus Stage and No Static at All, as well as the full Heroic clear. Collect five Golden Orbs during this run; simply moving through an orb is insufficient, so right-click it while within reach.\n\n8. For the orbs, inspect the first bridge's outer edge, the ledge behind Grand Vizier Ertan beside his slipstream, both sides of the Howling Gale bridge, and the spiral ramp toward Asaad. The map marks possible search positions, not guaranteed spawns. Jump toward an orb and click in midair; falling returns you to the entrance, whose unlocked slipstream shortens the return. Two alternatives float above Altairus and require his active tornadoes to lift you: leave him alive if you need those.\n\n9. At Asaad, kill him before Static Cling if your damage permits. Otherwise jump so you are airborne when each Static Cling cast completes, avoid the debuff throughout the fight, and finish him for No Static at All. Confirm both challenges and the Heroic final-boss credit before leaving.\n\n10. LOST CITY OF THE TOL'VIR: enter the ground-level portal in southern Uldum, around 60.5,64.4. At Lockmaw, hold damage and let five waves of four Frenzied Crocolisks accumulate. Kite them without killing them, then kill all 20 in a ten-second window for Acrocalypse Now. Finish Lockmaw and Augh afterward.\n\n11. High Prophet Barim - Kill It With Fire!: first wait for his red phoenix to leave fire patches. Carefully reduce Barim to 50% to enter the spirit phase without killing him. Use a lower-level helper if a bare-handed hit is lethal; the Midnight comments also describe controlled Oil of Immolation damage followed by Goblin Dragon Gun, Mark II. Cancel damaging effects as soon as the phase starts.\n\n12. In Barim's spirit phase, make Soul Fragments pass through the existing fire before killing them. Keep the purple Harbinger alive until three burning fragments are credited; it can consume fragments that reach it. Standing by a fire patch helps ignite fresh spawns immediately. Once the achievement appears, kill the Harbinger and finish Barim.\n\n13. Siamat - Headed South: leave the three large melee Servants of Siamat alive as they spawn; the small caster Minions do not give the required buff. Stand in melee range when each Servant dies to receive Lightning Charge. Kill the last-spawned Servant to remove Siamat's shield, then kill the other two close together while maintaining all three stacks. Confirm three Lightning Charges on YOUR character before killing Siamat; do not kill all adds from range.\n\n14. HALLS OF ORIGINATION: enter the pyramid in eastern Uldum, around 69.1,52.9. Temple Guardian Anhuur - I Hate That Song: a high-level immediate kill avoids the hymn entirely. If he shields, pull both pit levers and interrupt the exposed boss's Reverberating Hymn within 15 seconds. Put one player at each lever and clear/control the snakes so their hits do not interrupt the channels.\n\n15. Earthrager Ptah - Straw That Broke the Camel's Back: clear the sand-area trash FIRST, then click one of the dungeon's camels and fight Ptah while riding it. Avoid the dark Earth Spike marks and swirling Quicksand, which dismount you. Finish the boss without losing your camel; summoning an ordinary camel mount does not replace the encounter vehicle.\n\n16. Faster Than the Speed of Light: when ready, tell Brann to open the Vault of Lights. Immediately go around its four corners and kill all four Elemental Warders within five minutes, allowing time for the door-opening dialogue. Skip unnecessary Trogg packs; Anraphet himself does not have to die inside that timer. For Sun of a...., kill Rajh before he completes a recharge, interrupting his casts if your damage is low. Finish the Heroic final-boss requirement.\n\n17. DEADMINES: enter the mine building in Moonbrook, Westfall (about 42.6,71.7), follow the tunnels down and use the Heroic instance portal. Glubtok - Ready for Raiding: avoid his rotating Fire Wall; a quick kill before it appears is sufficient.\n\n18. Helix - Rat Pack: leave his Lumbering Oaf alive and let its charges smash into the lumber piles. Target the Mine Rats that emerge and kill them until you have 20. Do not AoE the Oaf down before the rats spawn. The rat counter can accumulate across attempts; check the achievement before finishing the encounter.\n\n19. Foe Reaper 5000 - Prototype Prodigy: keep the friendly Prototype Reaper above 90% health during the boss encounter. At high level, leave it safely upstairs, clear the enemies that activate the boss and kill Foe Reaper quickly. You do not have to bring the friendly vehicle into the damaging floor fight.\n\n20. Admiral Ripsnarl - It's Frost Damage: reduce him carefully below 75%, stop attacking, and let the fog phase continue. Leave the Vapors alive until three have grown and cast Coalesce. A high-level character can survive their explosions; lower-level players can hide in the cabin for each cast. Wait for achievement credit before killing Ripsnarl.\n\n21. Captain Cookie - I'm on a Diet: let Cookie climb into his pot and throw food. Eat ONE rotten green-glowing food to obtain a single Nauseated stack, then kill him immediately without gaining a second stack. The comment replies warn that killing him before the encounter initializes can miss credit even with zero stacks.\n\n22. Vigorous VanCleef Vindicator: after Cookie, click Vanessa's letter on the deck. When her nightmare starts, use the steam valves to escape the opening trap and run back toward the ship through each nightmare section. Avoid fire and rotating lightning, kill the required nightmare enemies, and protect the friendly NPCs in the Ripsnarl section before advancing. Reach and ENGAGE Vanessa within five minutes of the Nightmare Elixir; the timer is for engaging her, not killing her. Finish her for the Heroic clear.\n\n23. SHADOWFANG KEEP: enter the castle in southern Silverpine Forest (44.9,67.8) on Heroic. Baron Ashbury - Pardon Denied: kill him before Stay of Execution, or interrupt that heal immediately after Asphyxiate and heal yourself. Letting even one healing tick through fails the challenge. Lord Springvale - To the Ground!: kill him quickly, or kill/interrupt his adds before they grant him Unholy Empowerment.\n\n24. Lord Godfrey - Bullet Time: hold boss damage and let him summon Bloodthirsty Ghouls. When he channels Pistol Barrage, move so the ghouls follow you through the cone and die to HIS bullets. Repeat until 12 are credited, then kill him. Do not AoE the ghouls yourself; standing on the stairs does not make you immune to his barrage.\n\n25. GRIM BATOL: enter the portal in western Twilight Highlands, around 19.2,54.2, on Heroic. Finish the dungeon for 4844. At Erudax, for Don't Need to Break Eggs to Make an Omelet, kill both Faceless Corruptors immediately when they appear, before either reaches and damages an egg. High-level burst can end Erudax before that wave. The removed Umbrage for Umbriss challenge is not a prerequisite for this mount.\n\n26. THRONE OF THE TIDES: travel to the Abyssal Breach in northern Abyssal Depths, Vashj'ir (about 70.5,29.9), swim down into the giant whirlpool and enter on Heroic. Complete the current dungeon through Ozumat for Cataclysm Dungeon Hero. The old Old Faithful and Prince of Tides mechanics are not required by 4845 anymore, so do not look for removed versions of those encounters.\n\n27. Reopen 4845 and 4844. Finish any unchecked boss challenge or Heroic dungeon on another eligible character or the next daily reset as needed. When the meta completes, check the Mount Journal and achievement reward mail for Reins of the Volcanic Stone Drake, then learn it.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=62900",
    },
