        name = "Phosphorescent Stone Drake",
        mountCategory = "Rare Drops",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - An unpredictable rare spawn, competition and separate world phases make the search potentially lengthy.\n\n1. Reach Deepholm through your faction capital's Cataclysm portal. If the portal is not unlocked, follow the Deepholm introduction, starting with The Maelstrom, until you reach the Temple of Earth. Bring flying and a safe way to handle falling after an aerial pull.\n\n2. Search all six marked areas around the Temple of Earth: 42.0,43.6; 43.0,50.8; 49.1,55.6; 50.5,63.5; 53.7,39.7; and 55.1,54.1. Look above and below your current altitude, roughly around Stonecore-entrance height and the surrounding floating pillars. These are search centers, not guaranteed spawn positions.\n\n3. Use /target Aeonaxx while checking the areas, and visually inspect the dragon if targeted. A rare-alert addon can help, but remaining motionless at Stonecore does not cover every spawn or height. Check different valid War Mode or Chromie Time phases only with characters eligible for those phases; changing phase does not force a spawn.\n\n4. When Aeonaxx is present, get within range and attack him directly. On a low-level Chromie Time character he can hit hard, so bring help rather than assuming the old low-health vehicle encounter still applies. If sharing a find, assemble the small party and nearby eligible characters before the kill.\n\n5. Kill Aeonaxx, reach his corpse safely and loot Reins of the Phosphorescent Stone Drake. Stay in the same group and phase until looting is complete. Use the reins; a short unsuccessful patrol does not start a fixed countdown to your next sighting.",
