        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - The encounters are easy at high level, but the mount is a rare drop with weekly loot limits.\n\n1. Travel to original Uldum. If necessary use Zidormi at 56.0,35.1 to leave the assault phase. Fly to the high floating platform over the southwest coast at 38.4,80.6. The entrance is Throne of the Four Winds, not the Vortex Pinnacle farther east.\n\n2. Choose a legacy Normal or Heroic raid difficulty before entering. On a high-level character, either raid size is sufficient; choosing 25-player does not create an additional weekly mount roll after a 10-player kill.\n\n3. Defeat Anshal, Nezir and Rohash on the three outer platforms. Use the wind bridges to move between them and kill the last two before the first finishes recovering. If one revives, finish the active bosses again within the recovery window.\n\n4. After the Conclave is dead, click the central wind funnel on an outer platform to reach Al'Akir. Defeat him; at the final transition the platform breaks and the encounter gives you flight.\n\n5. Fly to the floating Heart of Wind reward crystal near Al'Akir's center platform and open it. Check its loot for Reins of the Drake of the South Wind, then use the reins. His vanished body is not the reward container.\n\n6. If it does not drop, repeat after the weekly raid reset or on another eligible character. Check Raid Info before returning: changing Normal to Heroic or 10 to 25 does not refresh this character's Al'Akir loot.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=63041",
    },
    [88746] = {
        category = "Dungeon and Raids",
        source = "Slabhide - The Stonecore",
        npcId = 43214,
        description = "A rare drop from Stonecore's second boss, farmable repeatedly on Normal.",
        difficulty = "medium",
