        itemId = 63046,
        name = "Grey Riding Camel",
        mountCategory = "Rare Drops",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Rare figurines are scattered across many locations and most are the dust-producing decoy.\n\n1. Travel to Uldum and speak to Zidormi near 56.0,35.1 if the N'Zoth assault is active. Choose the earlier Uldum. Ramkahen reputation and buying the Brown or Tan Riding Camel do not unlock the rare figurine.\n\n2. Enable friendly NPC nameplates. The figurine is tiny and cannot be reliably found by an old /target macro. An optional Camel Spotter addon can alert on its nameplate and distinguish the real figurine, NPC 50409, from the dust-producing 50410.\n\n3. Fly low over the marked Uldum search locations and inspect the exact ground, ledges, bushes and rooftops. All figurine pins belong to this step. They are possible locations, so an empty point is expected; sweep the whole route rather than waiting only beside Ramkahen.\n\n4. Click any figurine you find. Most crumble into Crumbled Statue Remnants; clear the fake and resume later patrols. The real figurine creates a cyclone and transports you to the Steam Pools in Feralas, applying Dormus' Rage for 20 minutes. No camel purchase is needed before clicking it.\n\n5. After the teleport, swim to shore and locate Dormus the Camel-Hoarder near 69.5,73.2 in the special Feralas phase. Defeat him and loot the reins before Dormus' Rage expires. Remain in the encounter phase until you have looted; old instructions to realm-hop for repeated kills are obsolete.\n\n6. Use the reins to learn the Grey Riding Camel and receive the associated Camel-Hoarder reward. If a sweep finds nothing, repeat later or check another legitimately available character phase. There is no guaranteed number of figurines or fixed successful time of day.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=63046",
    },
