        mountCategory = "Other",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A very rare project after substantial Archaeology preparation can require hundreds of Tol'vir solves.\n\n1. Learn Archaeology and raise its skill. For direct Tol'vir fragments, reach 450 and survey the active Tol'vir dig sites in Uldum. Complete other Kalimdor dig sites when necessary to create more chances for Uldum sites.\n\n2. If Uldum is showing the N'Zoth assault, speak to Zidormi near Ramkahen (56.0,35.1) to use the earlier Uldum phase for the original archaeology route. Dig-site boundaries rotate; a static pin cannot stand in for your active dig-site map.\n\n3. For the more consistent crate route, reach Archaeology 600 and Lorewalkers Exalted. Go to the Seat of Knowledge above Mogu'shan Palace (83.5,31.0 in the Vale), buy Brann's Mantid Artifact Hunter's Kit for 2 Restored Artifacts and use the map included in it while its locator is active.\n\n4. Survey Mantid sites in Townlong Steppes and Dread Wastes, solve the common artifacts and crate those completed objects into Restored Artifacts. The locator lasts 24 real-time hours; obtain another kit when its effect expires if you want to continue that route.\n\n5. Return to Brann and buy Crates of Tol'vir Archaeology Fragments with the Restored Artifacts. Open the crates, solve the current Tol'vir project, and repeat. Optional Tol'vir Hieroglyphics speed up solves that offer keystone sockets, but buying them does not improve the chance of discovering the Scepter.\n\n6. When Scepter of Azj'Aqir becomes the current project, complete its 150-fragment requirement, using up to three keystones if desired. Solve it, use the Scepter from your bags and check Ultramarine Qiraji Battle Tank in the Mount Journal.",
